5c2c8f2",54,-1,1,"stylistic - could move this into a method so we don't have duplicate code."],["8b5631d2_914d7fa5",55,-1,1,"I don't think the view should have access to the selection delegate, or the boomkark id. Instead the selection logic should be driven through BookmarkManagerMediator. The idea being that views are…"],["c7e82fb6_9606bf95",56,-1,1,"Do we have an updated asset for this? I thought it was temporary, I didn't realize the one we were using was already part of the code base. It doesn't seem to mesh well with the rest of the view…"],["f64076ab_668d5e0c",57,-1,1,"I don't think the selection delegate should be part of the property model. Instead you should poke at it from the mediator."],["ea16e4f0_b0a4624e",54,0,1,"rogue newline"]],0,125],[7257932,20441,295,7.601,6.192,[[8,1.0,22,297]],[["1c6dd89f_e539f184",55,-4,1,"The code you added here looks like a FSM, did you consider moving it to a dedicated class? Ideally we can drive this through the mediator to adhere to MVC."],["29b25e4e_b14dab45",55,-4,1,"We should move these ms timings into constants"],["5794df8a_403cead1",55,-4,1,"I wonder if this would make more sense to have the recycler view as a dependency. Relying on the parent view being a certain type here is implicitly coupling the two, and seems error prone to me."],["839ea40f_67005ed6",55,-4,1,"Can you add a comment why we don't consume the event in the move action but do for the other two?"],["d1f1edc2_68cd20b5",55,-4,0,"We start this runnable in the select runnable with the same delay as here - is there a case where we wouldn't have run mSelectRunnable, and get an ACTION_DOWN, and need to add this runnable again?"],["db89556a_3cca58e5",55,-4,0,"nit: I know this pre-dates all this work, but I think mSelectionEnabled is a bit misleading. Looking at the ViewBinder and code, this is expressing whether or not another row is selected / if there…"],["e069c664_1780d3cb",55,-4,1,"Is there a more robust way to express these interconnected timer events?"],["e8902602_dabf7403",55,-4,1,"Relying on the view holder seems wrong here."],["f5b8a54c_59579134",55,-4,1,"nit: here and above can be lambdas"],["3bbe541b_f4e1ab0a",54,-1,1,"nit: typo, s/IImprovedBookmarkRow/ImprovedBookmarkRow"],["a1605062_e985ac2b",58,-1,1,"Is there any other state we need to reset here, like the mIsLongPressTriggered, or the View's pressed state?"],["ed3e033d_4bc712d0",58,-1,1,"nit typo"],["07346c53_0c4da91a",54,0,1,"mContext?"],["3e3edabb_38d08e08",58,0,1,"Would these be better suited to be instance methods now? Then reference them through this::startDrag/startSelect?"],["4ba384f5_e22689b5",54,0,1,"According to BookmarkManagerDragHelper, this is nullable."],["a1f2d655_b85d58bc",58,0,0,"Why not `view#getHitRect(rect)` & `rect.contains(x,y)`?"],["ae917cfc_c22ceae9",54,0,1,"mSelectionDelegate?"],["fd92d9b3_e48ffbf7",54,0,0,"I think something should own this object. Right now it's kept around by the lambda reference on L659 I guess? We'll either need a manager class for all the instances, or add it into the property…"]],0,126],[7279479,20441,184,4.21,3.407,[[8,23]],[],0,127],[7293011,20448,210,4.21,3.407,[[8,0.745,24,157],[15,0.167,26,35],[3,0.088,52,18]],[["7dfb90a3_aac86f13",53,-4,0,"This loops through the entire RecyclerView when a selection state changes, which feels quite expensive... I wonder if we could just make the recycler view children a custom view that can handle…"],["d628aba3_588de2b8",59,-4,1,"Not a great fan of this traversal... it seems this section is meant to update the mouse icon during drag and drop. Since Android event dispatcher usually starts from the child, back to the parent, I…"],["f25882a2_d5606922",59,-4,1,"nit: Can you do [MotionEvent.obtain](https://developer.android.com/reference/android/view/MotionEvent#obtain(android.view.MotionEvent)) do copy the event?"],["089f259b_0f9ea4b4",59,0,1,"nit: Remove this comment line - it's not necessary a grab cursor, it could be other views that has the cursor icon set ;)"]],0,128],